                                        "sense_id": "c8f753de-073b-32fc-b654-1df775164229",
                                        "entry_id": "ba627024-09fc-3d90-90ba-4ebf9bd4055c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the United States of America and Canada"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe687869-ae4c-421f-8d14-9fa20da40b74",
                                                "sense_id": "c8f753de-073b-32fc-b654-1df775164229",
                                                "text": "Canado-American central districts have, to a large extent, been built after the advent of motorized transportation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9ee5fda-6924-4b01-ba9c-1c2fcac97fbc",
                                                "sense_id": "c8f753de-073b-32fc-b654-1df775164229",
                                                "text": "Following an Canado-American agreement, the CFS Mont-Apica changed vocation in 1958 to join to the air defence of North America (N.O.R.A.D.)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c0cbc2b-ed28-49f4-9d00-97e9c783d7fe",
                                                "sense_id": "c8f753de-073b-32fc-b654-1df775164229",
                                                "text": "The question as to whether the Anglo-American (and Canado-American) alliance delayed by the diasporas’ activism is an issue only if we assume that a security community leads necessarily to an alliance between its members -- otherwise, there is no reason to expect the U.S. and the British Empire to have allied before the First World War, and therefore to conclude that this ‘delay’ was caused by diasporas’ activism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4071a16b-58fc-4ed8-a4a7-6578652c1c37",
                                                "sense_id": "c8f753de-073b-32fc-b654-1df775164229",
                                                "text": "The Canado-American Association handled the situation in New Hampshire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63f4c3e3-150e-49bf-a2aa-6cf6467e357c",
                                                "sense_id": "c8f753de-073b-32fc-b654-1df775164229",
                                                "text": "The three markets concerned include Québec, the Canado-American market and the foreign countries market."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
